text It's fine.
text She answers instantly.
text @[Tomoya]
text You said it without hesitation...
sound C76.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text As long as I follow two rules, it's okay.
text @[Tomoya]
text What two rules?
sound C77.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I have to score highly on all tests, and I have to get into as good a college as possible.
text @[Tomoya]
text Most students here have those goals.
text This school awards scholarships to students who excel in sports and academics.
text An exceptional honor student is a great marketing wedge for them.
text @[Tomoya]
text So you're saying that your grades are so great that you don't need to take any classes.
sound C78.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text No, that's not true.
sound C79.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text There are some lectures I want to listen to, and they really want me to participate in certain classes.
text @[Tomoya]
text A little bit ago, a teacher pleaded with me to stay in class.
text I get competitive for no reason.
sound C7A.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Besides, you can't become an upstanding citizen if you don't study a lot.
text @[Tomoya]
text Hearing that from you sounds weird...
text I honestly can't tell if it's more or less convincing coming from her.
text @[Tomoya]
text How are your grades so good if you don't attend class?
text @[Tomoya]
text Does that mean you study at home?
sound C7B.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Yes...
